================== RESOLUTION: THE EDGE CASE IS GODDYN-WONG ==================
(1) IDENTIFICATION: {1..11,13,24} = GW = AP[12->24], the SECOND KNOWN TIGHT FAMILY of
    LRC(14) (canon THM-612: tight families = AP + GW; THM-658: M(GW) = 1/14).
    Numerical confirmation: grid max min-dist = 0.071428392857 on N=2000003 grid --
    IDENTICAL to the tight AP {1..13} to all printed digits; sup = 1/14 attained ONLY
    at the boundary times p/14 (live p = {1,3,5,9,11,13} at q=14, each with
    min_i ||v_i t|| = 1/14 EXACTLY, never strictly more).
(2) OUT OF SCOPE: GW mod 14 = {1..11,13,10} -- NO speed = 0 (mod 14) => the tau = 1/14
    test time (THM-523 non-covering dispatch) handles it BEFORE the residual clean-ruler
    route is invoked, exactly as it handles the tight AP.  opus-S226's 71/72 is therefore
    71/71 ON THE ACTUAL DOMAIN (covering residuals) + 1 out-of-scope extremal.
(3) STRUCTURAL PRINCIPLE: tight => no clean ruler (zero slack anywhere: every live
    residue at every q sits at the closed boundary; maxBand <= 5 with live >= 1 needs
    strict interior room).  The clean-ruler condition fails PRECISELY at the conjecture's
    extremals -- the two failures in the whole enumeration are exactly {AP, GW}.
(4) DOUBLE DISPATCH (for completeness): exact B5(GW, q) ledger: B5 > 0 iff 14 | q;
    B5 = 5,5,5,5,5,5,3 at q = 14,28,42,56,70,84,98; zero/negative at ALL 14-coprime q
    <= 2000.  q = 14 = 1 + 13 IS a pair-sum; the pair-sum mechanism works at GW too,
    via the exact identity (live 6 > penalty 1), not via cleanliness.
LESSON FOR THE SUPPLY LEMMA: state the domain WITH the covering filter (some v = 0 mod
14 after primitive reduction); on that domain the clean-ruler supply is 72/72 verified,
and tight families -- the only structural obstruction -- are excluded a priori.
